  "interpretation": "Topology-matched feedback has the lowest mean held-out error among the three restricted rules, but the cell-level intervals do not establish an advantage over either matched control. Its common-checkpoint gradient-direction diagnostic is also lower than both controls, showing that this descriptive metric and final learning need not order methods in the same way. The result places a boundary on anatomy-only routing in this seven-cell measured-response task.",
